@startuml
title Allpatek | Parcel registration and weather forecasts
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam dpi 120
hide footbox
actor Farmer
participant "Angular Webapp" as Web
participant "Spring REST API" as Api
participant "OpenStreetMap" as Maps
participant "Open-Meteo" as Weather

Farmer -> Web : Open /parcels/new with a local farmer profile
Web -> Maps : Embed selected coordinates in the map
Farmer -> Web : Save parcel details
Web -> Api : POST /api/v1/parcels
alt Parcel saved
  Api --> Web : Parcel resource
  Web --> Farmer : Return to /parcels
else Save fails
  Web --> Farmer : Keep the form visible and report failure
end

Farmer -> Web : Open /alerts
Web -> Api : GET /api/v1/parcels
Api --> Web : Parcel records
Web -> Web : Select owner's parcels with usable coordinates
alt Coordinates available
  Web -> Weather : GET forecast directly from the browser
  alt Forecast returned
    Weather --> Web : Current, hourly and daily data
    Web --> Farmer : Display readings and estimated risk
  else Forecast request fails
    Web --> Farmer : Display the weather error state
  end
else No eligible parcel, or parcel lookup failed
  Web --> Farmer : No forecast readings for this query
end
note over Web,Weather : Spring also exposes GET /api/v1/alerts and its own weather adapter.\nThe Angular alerts screen uses the direct Open-Meteo path shown above.
@enduml
